From e16105e36c4b35bfcd363b8b852ccb8de84bcb9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:56:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/11] feat(bench): opt-in robust statistics and interleaved
 comparison groups

Existing benchmarks print as before. Opting in gives:

- `min_sample(d)`: calls per sample calibrated once so a sample lasts at least `d`, one warm-up sample discarded, times per call;
- median with a distribution-free 95 % interval from order statistics (exact binomial ranks) and the relative MAD;
- `compare<R>(name, cases, scale, minSample)`: R rounds, each sampling every case once in a freshly shuffled order, so drifts hit all cases alike;
  returns per case the statistics above and the paired ratio to the first case (median of same-round ratios with its interval).

```cpp
const auto stats = ::benchmark::compare<40>("fft 1024", {{"SimdFFT", a}, {"StockhamFFT", b}}, 1024UZ, 5ms);
const bool faster = stats[1].ratio_to_reference.ci_high < 1.0;
```

### Changes
- `bench/benchmark.hpp`: `min_sample`, `compare`, `utils::median_ci_ranks`, `compute_robust_statistics`, `compute_ratio_statistics`
- `bench/qa_benchmark.cpp`: ranks checked against an exact binomial CDF, MAD, paired ratios
